   3: -- (spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience): server attempt fencing for
   4: -- keyed message creates.
   5: --
   6: -- Model. Every keyed send (messages.client_message_id, migration
   7: -- 20261005000414) is identified by (sender_id, conversation_id,
   8: -- client_message_id). A Phase 5 client dispatches each try of a key as an
   9: -- ATTEMPT with a monotonic generation (1, 2, ...). The server keeps, per key,
  10: -- one row in private.message_send_attempts:
  11: --   * fence_generation: the highest generation seen from a fence call or a
  12: --     generation-carrying create; NULL = no fence state (D4).
  13: --   * committed_at / message_id: the key's DELIVERY RECORD â€” when a message
  14: --     was last committed under the key and that message (SET NULL when it is
  15: --     deleted, committed_at kept). Written by every keyed insert path (the
  16: --     fenced create, the raw-insert trigger), by a fence or replay that finds
  17: --     an untracked stored message, and backfilled here for keyed messages
  18: --     created before this migration (messages already deleted before it leave
  19: --     no record: a fence then reports not_stored and a newer attempt may
  20: --     create the message again).
  21: --   * composition: the ORIGINAL submitted composition of the committed message
  22: --     (normalized by the route: trimmed content, effective type or null for
  23: --     attachment messages, reply target, sorted attachment ids; T4 adds sorted
  24: --     requested mention ids). Replays are compared against it; rows without one
  25: --     (messages created before this migration or by a raw insert) fall back to
  26: --     the stored message.
  27: --
  28: -- Functions (service_role only; the routes authorize the caller first):
  29: --   * public.fence_message_attempt(sender, conversation, key, generation):
  30: --     locks the key row (creating it when absent) and, in that transaction,
  31: --     returns 'superseded' when generation < fence_generation (nothing is
  32: --     written); otherwise raises fence_generation to the given generation and
  33: --     returns 'stored' + message_id when the key's message is committed
  34: --     (recording its delivery when untracked), 'stored' with a null message_id
  35: --     when the key's delivered message was deleted since (so a client never
  36: --     resends a message its sender deleted), else 'not_stored'. It never
  37: --     creates a message. The create route calls it first for every
  38: --     generation-carrying create, so a newer attempt that has reached the
  39: --     server fences every older generation before its INSERT.
  40: --   * public.create_message_attempt(...): creates a keyed text message, or a
  41: --     message (keyed or not) with 1-5 pending uploads (the former body of
  42: --     create_message_with_attachments, Phase 4 T12/T15). After the INSERT â€”
  43: --     i.e. immediately before commit, because PostgREST commits as soon as the
  44: --     function returns â€” it locks the key row and refuses to commit
  45: --     (ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED, whole transaction rolled back: no message, no
  46: --     attachment link, uploads stay pending) when
  47: --       - the create carries a generation lower than fence_generation, or
  48: --       - the create carries no generation (Phase 4 client) and fence state
  49: --         exists for the key (D4);
  50: --     and it refuses a generation-carrying create (MESSAGE_DELETED, rolled
  51: --     back) when the key's delivered message was deleted since, so an outbox
  52: --     retry never resurrects a message its sender deleted (a generation-less
  53: --     create keeps the Phase 4 behavior and creates it again); otherwise it
  54: --     records the delivery, the composition and (for a generation-carrying
  55: --     create) the generation, then commits. A replay of an already-stored key
  56: --     is not an insertion: it returns the stored message id and composition
  57: --     (created=false) and records an untracked delivery; a generation-carrying
  58: --     replay older than fence_generation raises ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED; a
  59: --     generation-less replay always answers like Phase 4.
  60: --   * public.create_message_with_attachments (Phase 4 signature, kept for
  61: --     older builds) now delegates to create_message_attempt without a
  62: --     generation or composition, so it obeys the same D4 rule.
  63: --
  64: -- Keyed writes outside the fenced contract (review T2 r1 finding 1):
  65: --   * send_message_as_self (client INSERT under RLS) additionally requires
  66: --     client_message_id IS NULL: clients cannot insert keyed messages
  67: --     directly (unkeyed client inserts keep their previous policy; no shipped
  68: --     build inserts messages from the browser â€” every build creates through
  69: --     the service-role create route).
  70: --   * trigger messages_client_message_id_immutable (BEFORE UPDATE OF
  71: --     client_message_id, conversation_id, sender_id): no role may set, change
  72: --     or clear a key after insert, nor move a keyed message to another
  73: --     conversation or sender (42501 CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_IMMUTABLE); the sender
  74: --     FK's ON DELETE SET NULL stays allowed. No shipped build updates these
  75: --     columns; message edits update content/status/is_edited only.
