## T3 â€” Fail-closed create and fence budgets with winning-insert quota
Reasoning: D1 makes replays quota-free, which needs separate, non-bypassable budgets; the current limiter is fail-open 
and counts attempts, not insertions.
Task: The insertion quota is charged in the same transaction as a winning insertion (once among concurrent same-key 
requests; never more stored messages than the quota with distinct keys at the boundary; not charged for replays); 
every authenticated create request â€” including malformed bodies, early-validation failures, replays, and quota 
losers â€” consumes a per-user request budget whose charge survives an insertion rollback; fence/lookup calls consume 
their own per-user budget (replacing the T2 fail-open 'message:fence' limiter, including the fence step inside a 
generation-carrying create); any exhausted budget returns 429; a budget that cannot be checked refuses the request as 
429 (D4 planning decision).
Done when: The AC-009 route-level clauses hold on the local database, including under a real limiter 
permission/availability failure.
Verify by: Messaging DB integration tests for each AC-009 route clause plus malformed-body and early-validation 
charging, rollback survival, and a limiter failure (revoked/unavailable function) producing 429 on create and on 
fence; the bound on growth of `private.message_send_attempts` (budgets or a retention rule) is stated in TRACK; Phase 
4/legacy compatibility tests pass; RLS review gate recorded.
Covers: FR-008, AC-009, AC-035
Root: T3
Depends on: T2

## T4 â€” Server-validated atomic mentions and current-member roster
Reasoning: Mentions are a data contract consumed by composer and notifications on both create paths; the autocomplete 
needs a current roster no existing read provides.
Task: A mention store holds application user IDs mentioned by a message, written in the same transaction as the first 
creation on both the text path and the attachment/voice path, only for conversation members at that time other than 
the sender; requested mention IDs are part of the stored original composition (changed mentions on replay â†’ 409; 
unchanged replay after a recipient left returns the stored message); only members can read mention records; no client 
can write them; messages fetched by members carry their mention IDs. An authorized read returns a conversation's 
current members (from `conversation_members`, so removed members are excluded) to members only.
Done when: The AC-024 server clauses, the AC-046 replay clause, and the roster contract hold on the local database for 
both create paths.
Verify by: Messaging DB integration tests: non-member and self IDs store nothing; changed-mention replay 409 with no 
change; forced mention-storage failure stores neither message, attachment links, nor mentions (text and attachment 
paths); anon/non-member read denied; direct client writes denied; unchanged replay after removal returns stored 
message; roster excludes a removed member and is denied to non-members; Phase 4/legacy compatibility passes; RLS 
review gate recorded.
